  "prediction": "**CBS News Overhauls \"The Early Show\" with New Team**\n\nIn a bid to boost ratings, CBS News has made significant changes to its morning program, \"The Early Show.\" The show's co-hosts, Harry Smith and Maggie Rodriguez, along with weather forecaster Dave Price, have been replaced by a new team.\n\nChris Wragge and Erica Hill, who have been co-anchors of the Saturday edition of \"The Early Show\" since 2008, will take over as co-anchors of the weekday show starting January 3. Jeff Glor, who has been anchoring the network's Saturday newscast, will join the team as the regular news reader. Marysol Castro, a former weather anchor for ABC's \"Good Morning America\" weekend edition, will serve as the new weather anchor.\n\nThe changes come as \"The Early Show\" continues to struggle in the ratings, consistently ranking behind NBC's \"Today\" show and ABC's \"Good Morning America.\" Despite the challenges, CBS News President Sean McManus is optimistic about the new team, citing their chemistry and ability to shift between hard news and lighter fare.\n\nHarry Smith, who had the longest tenure on \"The Early Show,\" will remain at the network as a news reporter and primary substitute anchor for Katie Couric's evening newscast, \"Face the Nation,\" and \"Sunday Morning.\" Smith expressed gratitude for his time on the show and wished the new team well.\n\nThe sudden changes have been met with mixed reactions, with some critics praising the move as a necessary shake-up, while others see it as a sign of desperation. The new team is set to debut on January 3, and it remains to be seen whether they will be able to boost the show's ratings.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n* Harry Smith and Maggie Rodriguez replaced by Chris Wragge and Erica Hill as co-anchors\n* Dave Price replaced by Marysol Castro as weather anchor\n* Jeff Glor joins as regular news reader\n* Harry Smith becomes primary substitute anchor for Katie Couric's evening newscast, \"Face the Nation,\" and \"Sunday Morning\"\n* New roles for Maggie Rodriguez and Dave Price to be determined",
